{"id":"e200fb70-289f-4985-a893-9aded53bd87b","object":"chat.completion","created":1784884600,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\"implementation\":\"def solve(case):\\n    threshold = case['threshold']\\n    calls = case['calls']\\n    accepted_call_ids = []\\n    diagnostics = []\\n    for call in calls:\\n        call_id = call['call_id']\\n        gain = call['loss_without_call'] - call['loss_with_call']\\n        prediction_tokens = call['prediction_tokens']\\n        if prediction_tokens <= 0:\\n            raise ValueError(\\\"prediction_tokens must be positive\\\")\\n        normalized_gain = gain / prediction_tokens\\n        accepted = call['parseable'] and normalized_gain >= threshold\\n        diagnostics.append({\\n            'accepted': accepted,\\n            'call_id': call_id,\\n            'normalized_gain': normalized_gain\\n        })\\n        if accepted:\\n            accepted_call_ids.append(call_id)\\n    return {\\n        'accepted_call_ids': accepted_call_ids,\\n        'diagnostics': diagnostics\\n    }\"}","reasoning_content":"We are implementing solve(case) for agent-task \"AGENT-TF-01\". The task: Toolformer API-call filtering. Input: case contains threshold and calls list. Each call has call_id, loss_without_call, loss_with_call, prediction_tokens, parseable. Output must match schema: accepted_call_ids (list of call_id strings) and diagnostics (list of dicts with accepted, call_id, normalized_gain). Normalized gain: (loss_without_call - loss_with_call) / prediction_tokens? The description: \"For each call subtract loss with the call from loss without it. Normalize gain by at least one prediction token.\" So gain = loss_without_call - loss_with_call. Then normalized_gain = gain / prediction_tokens. Then condition: parseable must be True and normalized_gain >= threshold. Note: The description says \"Require both parseability and normalized gain at or above threshold.\" Also \"Normalize gain by at least one prediction token.\" Means divide by prediction_tokens. So normalized_gain = (loss_without_call - loss_with_call) / prediction_tokens. Then accepted if parseable and normalized_gain >= threshold.\n\nOutput diagnostics in same order as calls input. Also accepted_call_ids list in order of accepted? But schema doesn't specify order; but diagnostics order is call order, and accepted_call_ids likely in order of appearance. We'll preserve input order.\n\nImplementation: iterate over case[\"calls\"] (list). For each, compute normalized_gain. Check if parseable and normalized_gain >= threshold. Then populate diagnostics list with accepted boolean, call_id, normalized_gain. For accepted_call_ids list, append call_id if accepted.\n\nReturn dict with accepted_call_ids and diagnostics.\n\nEdge cases: prediction_tokens could be zero? According to schema not specified, but we assume positive integer. If zero, division by zero -> raise? But input fixtures have positive. We'll trust but maybe handle as ValueError.\n\nWe must not mutate case. Use deep copy? Not needed as we don't modify. We'll read only.\n\nWe'll implement as function def solve(case): ... return result.\n\nNow format response: single JSON object with key \"implementation\" and value as JSON-escaped Python string. Need to escape newlines, backslashes, quotes.\n\nWrite Python code:\n\ndef solve(case):\n    threshold = case['threshold']\n    calls = case['calls']\n    accepted_call_ids = []\n    diagnostics = []\n    for call in calls:\n        call_id = call['call_id']\n        gain = call['loss_without_call'] - call['loss_with_call']\n        prediction_tokens = call['prediction_tokens']\n        if prediction_tokens <= 0:\n            raise ValueError(\"prediction_tokens must be positive\")\n        normalized_gain = gain / prediction_tokens\n        accepted = call['parseable'] and normalized_gain >= threshold\n        diagnostics.append({\n            'accepted': accepted,\n            'call_id': call_id,\n            'normalized_gain': normalized_gain\n        })\n        if accepted:\n            accepted_call_ids.append(call_id)\n    return {\n        'accepted_call_ids': accepted_call_ids,\n        'diagnostics': diagnostics\n    }\n\nBut note: gain could be negative? Not prohibited. normalized_gain could be negative. Condition >= threshold with threshold 0.05 could be false for negative. That's fine.\n\nCheck output schema: normalized_gain type number, can be float.\n\nNow test on first case: call0: loss_without 1.48911432, loss_with_call 0.30132987, gain=1.18778445, tokens=5, norm=0.23755689 >=0.05 true, parseable true => accept. call1: similar accept. call2: accept. call3: gain=1.18850153, tokens=3, norm=0.3961671767 accept. call4: gain=1.30384712, tokens=6, norm=0.217307853 accept. call5: parseable false => not accept. So accepted IDs: call0-4. Good.\n\nNow produce final JSON.\n\nNeed to ensure the Python string is properly escaped. Write the Python as a string, then encode as JSON value.\n\nWe'll produce: {\"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    threshold = case['threshold']\\n    calls = case['calls']\\n    accepted_call_ids = []\\n    diagnostics = []\\n    for call in calls:\\n        call_id = call['call_id']\\n        gain = call['loss_without_call'] - call['loss_with_call']\\n        prediction_tokens = call['prediction_tokens']\\n        if prediction_tokens <= 0:\\n            raise ValueError(\\\"prediction_tokens must be positive\\\")\\n        normalized_gain = gain / prediction_tokens\\n        accepted = call['parseable'] and normalized_gain >= threshold\\n        diagnostics.append({\\n            'accepted': accepted,\\n            'call_id': call_id,\\n            'normalized_gain': normalized_gain\\n        })\\n        if accepted:\\n            accepted_call_ids.append(call_id)\\n    return {\\n        'accepted_call_ids': accepted_call_ids,\\n        'diagnostics': diagnostics\\n    }\"}\n\nBut need to escape: newl